{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1428 -First 12; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1490 -First 12; Get-Content docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1634 -First 8; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1416 -First 18; Get-Content docs/test/test-cases.toml | Select-Object -Skip 1358 -First 10'","aggregated_output":"title = \"Terminal lane outcomes (handback + quarantine)\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/handback.py\"\r\ncode_symbol = \"close_partial/quarantine/report_path/render_report/_restore/diff_records\"\r\ndetail = \"\"\"close_partial: commits the lane's work as-is, moves each claimed spec to the TERMINAL partial/ (nothing re-claims it, so nothing strands) and writes ONE IMMUTABLE per-close report under docs/handbacks/ naming the claimed outcome, the reason, the commit range and the keep/discard split. The report is the close EVENT's identity — immutable so it never moves, unique so a second close is a second document — which is what dissolves the starvation class a mutable dedup proxy re-opens. A second close is refused rather than overwriting the first, and any refusal restores every report the call wrote; the terminal partial/ move alone is the anti-livelock property — the spec never returns to queued/, so the driver cannot claim, hand back and re-claim the same row forever. quarantine: the red arm - reverts the product paths to the merge base and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch under docs/work/handback/, reading `git diff --name-status -z` as three-field RECORDS so a rename cannot revert the wrong path, checking every git return code, and restoring rather than reporting when a revert step fails. Both leave the branch finished, so integrate.branch_outcomes reads the outcome off the spec's DIRECTORY - complete/=merged, cancelled/=cancelled, any open folder=handback - and every lane ends in a merge.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"Making the outcome the directory leaves no fourth answer and no state file that could hold one; partial work lands in trunk where a future WI can find it instead of on a branch nobody will look at.\"\"\"\r\ntest_refs = \"(see TC-138)\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nphase = 4\r\n\r\n[design.LLR-145]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]\r\ncode_symbol = \"_kind_action/_admission/_lane_count/gap_census\"\r\ndetail = \"\"\"The dispatcher's one scheduling decision (docs/concurrency-v2.md §A4/§A8), consuming schedule.kind_of - the §A1 classification's enforcement point. _kind_action is the ruled §A8 table verbatim per kind x human-held answer (`agent_common.human_holds`), and a human-held attestation/gate row SURFACES even under keep_nondependent — that dial answers whether OTHER lanes keep running, never whether the machine may approve; _admission is the barrier as a pure decision: any exclusive-kind frontier row stops new admission (wait) until every lane is back, then the first spine row admits alone as one exclusive assignment, and remaining spine rows wait for later exclusive turns, attestation/gate rows surface under attended (drain, exit 0 naming the open-items cards) and admit as the queued batch at single-approve's close; _lane_count resolves the lanes dial CLI > AGENT_LANES > stack.ini [agent-loop] > 1 (absent key = 1; the template seeds 2); gap_census is the empty-frontier ladder's rung-1 seam - unverified in-scope SRs, orphan rows and draft SNs from trace.analyze, handed to the intake mint helper (docs/concurrency-v2.md §A5.2), never minted in the lane.\"\"\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"The §A4.1 authority flip: admission replaced the claim rung's deleted safety_class refusal, so the policy must live at ONE decision point and be driven as a pure function.\"\"\"\r\ntest_refs = \"(see TC-143)\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nphase = 4\r\n\r\n[design.LLR-150]\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]\r\ntitle = \"Lane mechanics: worktree, worker subprocess, §A2 refresh subprocess\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py;project-trajectory/scripts/lane.py\"\r\nmodule = \"project-trajectory/scripts/handback.py\"\r\ncode_symbol = \"close_partial/render_report/report_path/_restore/_split_lines/_no_recursion_refusal\"\r\ndetail = \"`close_partial` writes the report FIRST (it is the event's identity), refuses when one already exists, and restores EVERY report this call wrote on any refusal — so a multi-spec lane cannot half-close. `intake._close_drafts` titles the disposition on the report PATH and nothing else, and says so LOUDLY when a terminal spec has no report rather than minting zero rows quietly. Every partial and cancelled close earns exactly one disposition row — a re-sweep mints none, a genuinely second close is a second report and so a second row, and a disposition row never mints a disposition for itself (refused at both ends); a complete close is spot-checked at the declared rate rather than gated; continuing partial work drafts a successor carrying explicit lineage that survives the id change, never re-opening a terminal row. A disposition that owes a successor drafts one or adopts an already-filed one that supersedes the disposed row.\"\r\nrationale = \"\"\"The path is the only token in the event's identity that cannot move. Folding the report's `claimed_outcome` in as well was rejected: it re-reads a MUTABLE field on every sweep, so one edit mints a second disposition for the same close — the starvation class returning through a new proxy.\"\"\"\r\ntest_refs = \"TC-156; TC-331\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\ncomponent = \"CMP-008\"\r\nphase = 5\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the dispatch admission suite: an exclusive row + a busy lane answers wait (never a parallel claim slipped past the barrier) while the same frontier without one keeps filling lanes; lanes back -> every spine row admits as ONE batch ahead of ordinary work; the §A8 table verbatim per kind x level (attended surfaces attestation/gate rows, single-approve keeps non-dependent work and admits the queued approval batch only at the close, autonomous dispatches them exclusive); the lanes ladder resolves CLI > AGENT_LANES > stack.ini > 1 with absent/malformed/sub-1 falling to serial; gap_census names unverified SRs, orphan rows and draft SNs mechanically and answers [] on a registry-less repo; kind_of agrees with classify at every quarantine.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies SR-148 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-149 admission-table detail contract\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_dispatch_admission.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 4\r\n\r\n[test.TC-144]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-156\", \"LLR-150\"]\r\nlevel = \"Integration\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the dispatch loop suite on real git repos with the real bar: each spine claim carries one work item in its one commit and its worker receives that item; a parked lane claimed with one item resumes, while a parked claim holding several items stops the run before any mutation or relaunch; ordinary work admits only after the exclusive turn closes; a NEEDS-HUMAN worker hands back, the lane's refresh runs as its own subprocess and the branch merges; a red refresh quarantines a merges-nothing branch once and stops the run for a done-asserting one; an attended gate row drains and exits 0 with the approvals banner; the empty-frontier ladder hands the gap census to the intake mint (rows minted in one bookkeeping commit, driven by the same run, deduped on the next idle pass) and counts rung-2 cards off the shared pending read; pause/dirty-trunk/stall/crash-resume keep their serial-loop contracts at lanes=1.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies SR-156 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-150 detail contract\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_dispatch.py\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 4\r\n[test.TC-138]\r\nverifies = [\"SR-144\", \"LLR-144\"]\r\nlevel = \"Unit\"\r\nmethod = \"\"\"Run the handback suite: a partial close moves each claimed spec to the terminal partial/ and writes its immutable per-close report under docs/handbacks/, leaves the branch finished, is CLEAN under the real trajectory check (R-A exempts partial — the spec's definition is deliberately byte-identical), refuses a second close without residue, and is LOUD when a terminal spec has no report; a close writes NO blockref because the partial/ folder is itself terminal (the anti-livelock property is the move, not a queued-plus-blockref marker), while an existing Deliverable survives the move; a branch trunk holds no claim for is refused. The quarantine arm reverts the product paths and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch, reverts a RENAME correctly (the --name-status -z stream read as records, not pairs - mutation-proven), leaves the handback bookkeeping alone, refuses when the red is not the lane's own code, and restores rather than reports when a revert step fails.\"\"\"\r\ntier = \"Full\"\r\nexpected = \"Satisfies SR-144 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-144 detail contract\"\r\nautomated = \"Yes\"\r\nevidence = \"tests/test_handback.py; tests/test_handback.py::test_a_partial_close_of_a_two_spec_claim_refuses_before_any_report; tests/test_handback.py::test_an_adjudication_close_of_a_two_spec_claim_refuses_before_any_move\"\r\nstatus = \"Approved\"\r\nphase = 4\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
