{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"rg -n -A 10 -B 1 'LLR-150' docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml; rg -n -A 8 -B 1 'TC-143|TC-138' docs/test/test-cases.toml\"","aggregated_output":"1419-code_symbol = \"run\"\n1420:detail = \"\"\"The scheduling front end a plain agent_loop.py launch runs, serial at lanes=1 (the lanes dial admits more lanes at once; each lane's mechanics are LLR-150's): each cycle re-derives the ready frontier (schedule.frontier), stops claiming under the tracked pause (a parked or finished lane still resumes and merges, and the run exits 8 once nothing is in flight), refuses on a dirty trunk at the cycle top while no lane is live (a change confined to agent_common.OWNER_ONLY_PATHS, the owner's scratchpad, is not dirt), resumes a parked claimed branch else claims the next queued WI in build order (integrate.claim, branch name check-ref-format-validated), launches one worker session on the claimed branch's worktree (agent_loop.py --worktree --wi with the session dials forwarded), merges each finished branch through the serial merge slot (integrate.integrate) counting the WIs merged, and stops loudly on any composed refusal once the live lanes drain - a stall aborts, an empty frontier drains to exit 0. A NEEDS-HUMAN worker does not stop the run: its lane hands back (the WI closes partial and merges) and the run drives on; an active/ directory with no branch ref is residue, not a refusal. The session-config preflight applies only when work needs a worker. Never pushes.\"\"\"\n1421-rationale = \"\"\"Ordering only, no new authority: every refusal stays where it already lives, and the driver is ~400 lines of composition against the 4,042-line dispatcher it replaces.\"\"\"\n1422-test_refs = \"(see TC-137)\"\n1423-status = \"Approved\"\n1424-component = \"CMP-008\"\n1425-phase = 4\n1426-\n1427-[design.LLR-144]\n1428-sr_refs = [\"SR-144\"]\n1429-title = \"Terminal lane outcomes (handback + quarantine)\"\n1430-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/handback.py\"\n--\n1498-\n1499:[design.LLR-150]\n1500-sr_refs = [\"SR-156\"]\n1501-title = \"Lane mechanics: worktree, worker subprocess, §A2 refresh subprocess\"\n1502-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dispatch.py;project-trajectory/scripts/lane.py\"\n1503-code_symbol = \"_admit_parked/_stop_run/ensure_worktree/worker_argv/spawn_worker/run_worker/spawn_refresh\"\n1504-detail = \"\"\"One lane's mechanics extracted from the dispatcher (docs/concurrency-v2.md §A4.2): ensure the lane worktree (integrate.lane_worktree, the one home both the worker and the refresh agree on), build the worker argv with the plain launch's session dials forwarded explicitly, launch the worker subprocess (spawn_worker non-blocking for the lane table and dispatch._launch's own default; run_worker its blocking form - a DECLARED SEAM with no in-kit caller, kept for a synchronous single-lane run, and the shape dispatch._launch's worker= injection substitutes), and run the §A2 station refresh as the lane's OWN subprocess (spawn_refresh - the invoker's integrate.py refresh CLI under the harness interpreter) so N lanes' bars overlap instead of queueing at the dispatcher (§A4.3). Reports outcomes, decides none: the tree signal (specs moved out of active/<branch>/) plus exit codes are the whole protocol - no state file, no back-channel.\"\"\"\n1505-rationale = \"\"\"The §A4.2 split keeps the deciding half (dispatch.py) apart from the running half, so at lanes=1 the dispatcher degenerates to the serial loop and the concurrency is a table size, not a second code path.\"\"\"\n1506-test_refs = \"(see TC-144)\"\n1507-status = \"Approved\"\n1508-component = \"CMP-008\"\n1509-phase = 4\n1358-\n1359:[test.TC-138]\n1360-verifies = [\"SR-144\", \"LLR-144\"]\n1361-level = \"Unit\"\n1362-method = \"\"\"Run the handback suite: a partial close moves each claimed spec to the terminal partial/ and writes its immutable per-close report under docs/handbacks/, leaves the branch finished, is CLEAN under the real trajectory check (R-A exempts partial — the spec's definition is deliberately byte-identical), refuses a second close without residue, and is LOUD when a terminal spec has no report; a close writes NO blockref because the partial/ folder is itself terminal (the anti-livelock property is the move, not a queued-plus-blockref marker), while an existing Deliverable survives the move; a branch trunk holds no claim for is refused. The quarantine arm reverts the product paths and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch, reverts a RENAME correctly (the --name-status -z stream read as records, not pairs - mutation-proven), leaves the handback bookkeeping alone, refuses when the red is not the lane's own code, and restores rather than reports when a revert step fails.\"\"\"\n1363-tier = \"Full\"\n1364-expected = \"Satisfies SR-144 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-144 detail contract\"\n1365-automated = \"Yes\"\n1366-evidence = \"tests/test_handback.py; tests/test_handback.py::test_a_partial_close_of_a_two_spec_claim_refuses_before_any_report; tests/test_handback.py::test_an_adjudication_close_of_a_two_spec_claim_refuses_before_any_move\"\n1367-status = \"Approved\"\n--\n1413-\n1414:[test.TC-143]\n1415-verifies = [\"SR-148\", \"LLR-149\"]\n1416-level = \"Unit\"\n1417-method = \"\"\"Run the dispatch admission suite: an exclusive row + a busy lane answers wait (never a parallel claim slipped past the barrier) while the same frontier without one keeps filling lanes; lanes back -> every spine row admits as ONE batch ahead of ordinary work; the §A8 table verbatim per kind x level (attended surfaces attestation/gate rows, single-approve keeps non-dependent work and admits the queued approval batch only at the close, autonomous dispatches them exclusive); the lanes ladder resolves CLI > AGENT_LANES > stack.ini > 1 with absent/malformed/sub-1 falling to serial; gap_census names unverified SRs, orphan rows and draft SNs mechanically and answers [] on a registry-less repo; kind_of agrees with classify at every quarantine.\"\"\"\n1418-tier = \"Full\"\n1419-expected = \"Satisfies SR-148 AcceptanceCriteria via the LLR-149 admission-table detail contract\"\n1420-automated = \"Yes\"\n1421-evidence = \"tests/test_dispatch_admission.py\"\n1422-status = \"Approved\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
