ting the first, and any refusal restores the one report the call wrote; the terminal partial/ move alone is the anti-livelock property � the spec never returns to queued/, so the driver cannot claim, hand back and re-claim the same row forever. quarantine: the red arm - reverts the product paths to the merge base and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch under docs/work/handback/, reading `git diff --name-status -z` as three-field RECORDS so a rename cannot revert the wrong path, checking every git return code, and restoring rather than reporting when a revert step fails. Both leave the branch finished, so integrate.branch_outcomes reads the outcome off the spec's DIRECTORY - complete/=merged, cancelled/=cancelled, any open folder=handback - and every lane ends in a merge.\"\"\"\r\nLLR-150 detail = \"\"\"One lane's mechanics extracted from the dispatcher (docs/concurrency-v2.md �A4.2): ensure the lane worktree (integrate.lane_worktree, the one home both the worker and the refresh agree on), build the worker argv for the lane's one work item with the plain launch's session dials forwarded explicitly, launch the worker subprocess (spawn_worker non-blocking for the lane table and dispatch._launch's own default; run_worker its blocking form - a DECLARED SEAM with no in-kit caller, kept for a synchronous single-lane run, and the shape dispatch._launch's worker= injection substitutes), and run the �A2 station refresh as the lane's OWN subprocess (spawn_refresh - the invoker's integrate.py refresh CLI under the harness interpreter) so N lanes' bars overlap instead of queueing at the dispatcher (�A4.3). A parked lane resumes only when its claim holds exactly one work item; a parked claim holding several stops the run by name before any mutation or relaunch. Reports outcomes, decides none: the tree signal (specs moved out of active/<branch>/) plus exit codes are the whole protocol - no state file, no back-channel.\"\"\"\r\nLLR-161 detail = \"`close_partial` writes the report FIRST (it is the event's identity), refuses when one already exists, and restores the one report it wrote on any refusal, so a refused close leaves no report behind. `intake._close_drafts` titles the disposition on the report PATH and nothing else, and says so LOUDLY when a terminal spec has no report rather than minting zero rows quietly. Every partial and cancelled close earns exactly one disposition row � a re-sweep mints none, a genuinely second close is a second report and so a second row, and a disposition row never mints a disposition for itself (refused at both ends); a complete close is spot-checked at the declared rate rather than gated; continuing partial work drafts a successor carrying explicit lineage that survives the id change, never re-opening a terminal row. A disposition that owes a successor drafts one or adopts an already-filed one that supersedes the disposed row.\"\r\nTC-143 method = \"\"\"Run the dispatch admission suite: an exclusive row + a busy lane answers wait (never a parallel claim slipped past the barrier) while the same frontier without one keeps filling lanes; lanes back -> the first spine row admits alone ahead of ordinary work and the other spine rows wait for later exclusive turns; the �A8 table verbatim per kind x level (attended surfaces attestation/gate rows, single-approve keeps non-dependent work while held attestation/gate rows drain and surface at keep-nondependent's close without releasing their hold, autonomous dispatches them exclusive one at a time); the lanes ladder resolves CLI > AGENT_LANES > stack.ini > 1 with absent/malformed/sub-1 falling to serial; gap_census names unverified SRs, orphan rows and draft SNs mechanically and answers [] on a registry-less repo; kind_of agrees with classify at every quarantine.\"\"\"\r\nTC-138 method = \"\"\"Run the handback suite: a partial close moves its one claimed spec to the terminal partial/ and writes its immutable per-close report under docs/handbacks/, leaves the branch finished, is CLEAN under the real trajectory check (R-A exempts partial � the spec's definition is deliberately byte-identical), refuses a second close without residue, and is LOUD when a terminal spec has no report; a close writes NO blockref because the partial/ folder is itself terminal (the anti-livelock property is the move, not a queued-plus-blockref marker), while an existing Deliverable survives the move; a claim holding no work item or several is refused before any report, move or commit; a branch trunk holds no claim for is refused. The quarantine arm reverts the product paths and keeps the failing diff as a bar-inert .patch, reverts a RENAME correctly (the --name-status -z stream read as records, not pairs - mutation-proven), leaves the handback bookkeeping alone, refuses when the red is not the lane's own code, and restores rather than reports when a revert step fails.\"\"\"\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
